				<wikidot:authorName>Witsfool</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2196708</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>From what I have observed in this ongoing debate of whether things should be -J or not, a -J designation is when something is written AS a joke. Not just because something happens to BE funny. There are many things in life that are completely real that happen to be enormously funny. So it would be dumb to believe that there wouldn't be &quot;real&quot; SCPs that happen to have amusing effects.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
