					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-142558#post-1786458</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-142558/scp-586#post-1786458</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 30 May 2013 19:02:53 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Garrey</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1618960</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This would work as a joke, but as it is, there's no Foundation personnel - even if influenced by its property of having a spelling error introduced whenever it's mentioned - that would draw up this document, accidentally have a picture of a &quot;green pope&quot; on their hard drive, select that, and not be aware of the error looking at the document (because you don't just need a picture of &quot;a green pope&quot; or whatever it's described as, you need an actual picture of SCP-586).<br /> And even if the reader strains his credulity and imagines a situation where the person who wrote the containment document would sent a request to a third person for a picture of the item and would try to refer to it as &quot;green pipe&quot; (instead of its SCP designation), on the off chance that that third person would actually send a picture of a &quot;green pope&quot;, that would, according to the description, still be recognised as a picture of the wrong item (since it's not written, but visual).</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
